[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-44", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 44 — IC05 served and gated (99 params, 0 disagreements), not admitted at 2.4 s/query; memberships resident", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-44.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 44 - IC05 served and gated, not admitted: 2.4 s a query\n\n> Seed: iteration 43's S23b (IC05 so INS5 has a covering read). Judge:\n> bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung :sf1-full; SUT levi (M4 4P+6E, 16\n> threads), driver judah, LAN.\n\n## Generate / Rank\n\n  The loader now reads forum_hasMember_person (1.61M rows) into the\n  shape INS5 already writes -- mb:<forum>:<person> with forum, person and\n  joinDate -- so loaded and streamed memberships are one population. The\n  SUT holds 25.4M quads in 6.2 GB used heap (was 20.6M / 5.2).\n\n  IC05 in the kotobase dialect: two reaches (friends; friends-of-friends\n  excluding self) as [forum post] pairs -- the post's creator ?x, its\n  forum ?f, and the membership reached by its DERIVED id through a\n  function clause `(str \"mb:\" ?f \":\" ?x)`: one point lookup per (person,\n  forum) pair instead of a scan of the person's memberships -- unioned\n  and counted per forum, top 20. A hand-written twin walks the same\n  index. Gate on the 99 official IC05 parameters: 0 disagreements\n  (4,780 checks in all).\n\n  Cost, in-thread on the first parameter: Datalog 2.3-2.7 s, twin\n  0.67-0.69 s. The shape is the cost: ~2,200 reached persons x ~300\n  posts each are candidates before the join date filters them. The\n  answer for that parameter is empty and correctly so -- its minDate\n  lies after the last loaded date; the joins it asks about arrive in\n  the INS5 stream.\n\n  Decision: served and gated, NOT admitted to the measured mix. At 2.4 s\n  a query it fails the 95% rule at any rate; admitting it would turn a\n  widening into a regression and call it growth.\n\n    rung sf1-full  slots  threads  reads/s  upd/s  on-time%  thru/s   SUT\n      it.43          64     16      3328     1475   100.00    4801.5   20.6M quads\n      it.44          64     16      3328     1475   100.00    4631.8   25.4M quads, memberships resident (3712: 49.2%)\n\n  The 11-op row is restated -3.5% for the larger live heap; the loader\n  keeps memberships because INS5 now lands on a real population.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - A covering read for INS5 exists now, but it cannot be used as one:\n    IC05's answer is a top-20 by post count, and a fresh membership with\n    no posts is outside that window by construction. The class stays\n    :no-covering-read, honestly.\n  - The plan IC05 needs starts from the other end -- memberships joined\n    after minDate (a value range on joinDate), then posts by (creator,\n    forum) without walking every post of the creator. That second step\n    is a composite index the datom plane does not have (S35), the same\n    kind of structure the grouped drive added for (creator, date).\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: served-op coverage 11 -> 12 (IC05\ngated), measured mix unchanged at 11; the row restated on a larger\nresident SUT (4631.8). Ratio to the audited No.1: 30.\n\nSeeds for iteration 45, in order:\n\n  - S35: IC05 from memberships first + a (creator, forum) order.\n  - S34: bindings as arrays inside the join.\n  - Owner: a SUT host (M4; SF3's 13 GB).\n"}]
